  _debugUncommonResourcePull: 3
  _debugRareResourcePull: 3
  _debugLandmarkPlan: Littoral Karst Landmark Plan
  _debugDominantLandmarkRole: karst arch or sea-stack crown
  _debugRouteUse: Player should chain visible stacks and arches without needing UI
    help.
  _debugEmotionalRead: Readable, exposed, and navigable without feeling harmless.
  _debugSpatialPattern: Littoral Karst Spatial Pattern
  _debugResourcePocketPattern: Loose scrap and easy basics sit around the feet of
    arches, stacks, and readable shelf lips.
  _debugNodeClusterPattern: Small mineral nodes hide in short wall cuts and at the
    base of obvious limestone breaks.
  _debugSafePocketPattern: Reorientation pockets appear often on the lee side of
    stacks and inside shallow arch shadows.
  _debugRouteAnchorPattern: Routes chain from one big karst silhouette to the next
    without needing UI help.
  _debugRareObjectivePattern: Rare value sits one ring deeper than the readable starter
    loop, still visible from a stable landmark.
  _debugExplorationLoop: Spot stack, clear pocket, grab one node, peek deeper, then
    return by the same silhouette chain.
  _debugWhyPlayerComesHere: Starter resources, readable routes, and fast landmark
    memory.
  _debugRouteClarity: 5
  _debugSafePocketFrequency: 5
  _debugRareRewardPull: 1
  _debugEncounterPressure: 1
  _debugHazardPressure: 1
  _debugVisitPurpose: Early exploration biome. Come here to learn routes, gather
    basics, and follow strong natural shapes and search obvious pockets.
  _debugCommonRewardHook: Common runs pay out in Titanium Scrap and Silica Shards.
  _debugRareRewardHook: 'Rare pull is modest: Fiber Kelp and Glass Panel.'
  _debugLandmarkIdentity: Archipelago Needles reads through spires, steps, and big
    natural crowns. Landmarks should feel bright and readable.
  _debugSafePocketIdentity: Reorientation pockets are frequent. The player should
    often see a clear reset point nearby.
  _debugRiskSummary: 'Main failure mode: bad drops and exposed lines. Creature pressure
    stays low.'
  _debugExtractionFocus: 'Loose pickup fields and readable shallow mineral nodes.
    Early tier: keep runs short and favor stone pockets and hard-form nodes.'
  _debugLandmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is karst arch or sea-stack crown. This
    slot should read through small limestone teeth and arch feet; use vertical forms
    to keep heading.
